From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jess <jessica.welsh.carter@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:06:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mproton: ntdll: Make steamclient trampolines writable without
 PROT_EXEC on arm64 hosts.

steamclient_setup_trampolines() made steamclient's .text RWX with
mprotect() and ignored the result. macOS on Apple Silicon refuses
PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC outside MAP_JIT mappings, so the pages stayed
read-only, writing the first jump faulted inside the unix call, and the
redirect to lsteamclient was silently dropped: games got Valve's
steamclient code. On an arm64 host steamclient is always x86 code run by
the emulator, so the host never executes those pages: ask for RW only.
Also report a failed mprotect instead of faulting.

Found with steam/tests/redirect (fake steamclient(64).dll): x86_64 and
i686 both faulted writing CreateInterface's trampoline.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index f8a55adb096..86c9c14d3da 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -1357,7 +1357,18 @@ static NTSTATUS steamclient_setup_trampolines( void *args )
         addr = (void *)(((UINT_PTR)src_mod + src_sec[i].VirtualAddress) & ~page_mask);
         size = (src_sec[i].Misc.VirtualSize + page_mask) & ~page_mask;
         if (noexec_cached) mprotect(addr, size, PROT_READ);
-        else mprotect(addr, size, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC);
+#ifdef __aarch64__
+        /* steamclient is x86 code, run by the emulator: the host never executes these
+         * pages, and macOS refuses PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC outside MAP_JIT mappings. */
+        else if (mprotect(addr, size, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE))
+#else
+        else if (mprotect(addr, size, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC))
+#endif
+        {
+            ERR( "mprotect %p-%p failed (%s), not redirecting steamclient to lsteamclient\n",
+                 addr, (char *)addr + size, strerror(errno) );
+            return STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED;
+        }
     }
 
     src_exp = get_module_data_dir( src_mod, IMAGE_FILE_EXPORT_DIRECTORY, NULL );
